From 67a4ffc996fc2834b86b6367df3903174e2783f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:41:48 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] Android: carve tool coroutine stacks from the Qt
 main-loop thread stack

The Android runtime rejects Java frames and JNI references outside the
calling thread's stack, so tool coroutines that open windows or dialogs
failed (invalid JNI transition reference, spurious StackOverflowError).
Coroutine stacks now come from a pool inside the main-loop thread's
(enlarged) stack.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
